{"id":"a1ebbcbe-6728-4650-af1f-866612b031bd","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8677615aae3a1c3a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/workspace-changes.ts","baseline":{"blob":"60338975a59b1b6d7194f90218b18ed84cbea9da","start":6323,"end":6357},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","pending","=","pendingOf","(","args","[","0","]",")"]},"context":{"before":"b9194ca3efb33852#7","after":"d56e6cf02cbbc5fd"}},"payload":{"text":"(a path this burst already has as added or changed — a write's own touch, as every write makes — reports\nnothing new: no stat to decide it, which is a whole path lookup in zen-fs; a repository's load made one\nfor every file it wrote)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:56:03.506Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:56:03.506Z"}
{"id":"e180d0e2-9778-414a-a210-b80e9c24dd19","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3bff037bca66f80c","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/workspace-changes.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7dd7140ce4fe19b75dfdf7d50334b21669902a27","start":1,"end":54},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","countCall",",","timeCall","}","from","\"","./fs-boundaries","\""]},"context":{"after":"dfa262d0f3c1295a"}},"payload":{"text":"The workspace's ONE change stream. The workspace is a zen-fs store in shared memory that several realms write\n(the editor through its FileSystemProvider, isomorphic-git and the terminal directly, node scripts and the preview\ndev server in the node worker) — and shared memory tells nobody anything. So each realm watches the mutating\noperations its own /workspace store performs and reports them, batched, as `workspace.changed` on the hub:\n\n• the workbench (workspace-fs.ts) persists every change to IndexedDB and announces it to VS Code — whoever wrote;\n• the node worker's dev servers hot-reload from it.\n\nWatched at the StoreFS level (below `fs`, which is a frozen module namespace), so no writer can go around it.\nA `touch` is a change only when it changes the size or the modification time — emptying a file is ONLY a touch\n(size 0) in zen-fs — while a read's access-time touch stays quiet.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:56:18.177Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:56:18.177Z"}
{"id":"ed349b1c-601f-49f8-a8c8-0a94a9ad361f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"aca07bfee3abdbfe","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/workspace-changes.ts","baseline":{"blob":"ab48b18eb4b804b9d2fe1f6a8cca2a6fe0842aff","start":4506,"end":4514},"shape":{"type":"Expression","atoms":["timeCall"]},"context":{"before":"05b5a1f0e7843bd8","after":"61ba869f8973c536#0"}},"payload":{"text":"(each batch counted, with its paths: the metrics plane's `fs`, fs-boundaries.ts — the time what hears it takes)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:56:07.706Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:56:07.706Z"}
